  "description": "Talk about set it and forget it: The only skill culturing your own buttermilk requires is patience.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 1 day 6 hr 5 min.\n\nNotes: You can make larger (or smaller) volumes as needed. I use a ratio of one tablespoon starter for every cup milk with reliable results. Unless your culture was not designed to be perpetuated (some freeze-dried options fall into this category), you can reserve a bit of each batch to culture the next.\nSome recipes indicate that you should pasteurize your milk (at 82°C) before culturing or at least warm it to 24°C. This step is entirely unnecessary, as store-bought milk is all pasteurized before it hits the shelves.",
